# Case 3 of the scenario guide: a decision the owner does not want made blindly. Two
# no-write lanes hold the same question; the council stays sealed until both return,
# and the Lead locks the decision with the rejected alternative in the rationale.
$ maestro work add "Session identity after pid reuse" --kind task --atomic-reason "one decision, no code" --acceptance "a locked decision with a falsifier"
w1 added: Session identity after pid reuse

$ maestro dispatch open w1 --lane decision --council-members 2 --objective "recommend how a session proves it is still the same process after the OS reuses its pid" --owned-scope "src/kernel/sessions.ts and its tests, read only" --excluded-scope "any code change" --mutation no-write --stop-condition "options, recommendation, and falsifier written" --evidence-required "source: note path with mechanism per option" --pane w1:pA
x1 [open]
work: w1
objective: recommend how a session proves it is still the same process after the OS reuses its pid
owned scope: src/kernel/sessions.ts and its tests, read only
excluded scope: any code change
mutation: no-write
stop condition: options, recommendation, and falsifier written
lane: decision
evidence required: source: note path with mechanism per option
pane: w1:pA
target session: none
opened by: test-session
claimed by: none
held by: none

